    	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8923" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8923"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8923' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8923'>10/23/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 12</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8923"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContainer callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8930" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h3 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8930">Update 29 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 12 About Proposed Project Timeline If Referendum Is Approved (October 23, 2026)</h3>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<div class="fsElement fsLayout fsTwoColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8931" data-use-new="true" >

						<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-1 fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8932"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_8933" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>The countdown is on to Election Day, and this week, we would like to answer another question we have heard from members of our community: <em><strong>If the referendum is approved, when would the construction work begin?</strong></em></p>

<p>If approved by voters, work would not begin on every project at the same time. Instead, the projects would be completed in phases, with bidding and construction scheduled to take advantage of ideal times during the school year and summer months while minimizing disruption to students and staff.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Whether you reside in Essex Fells, Fairfield, North Caldwell, or Roseland, your vote impacts the future of West Essex. If both ballot questions are approved the district will unlock $9.3 million in state aid to help offset the costs and reduce the tax impact. Based on the district&rsquo;s current preliminary schedule:&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li><u><strong>General Construction - May 2027 through January 2029</strong></u>: This would include the high school classroom addition and Media Center renovation, lower wall and window replacement, security vestibules, and interior and exterior door improvements.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<ul>
	<li><u><strong>Turf Field, Lighting and Stadium - May 2027 through September 2027</strong></u>: Construction would be concentrated primarily during the summer months when activity on campus is reduced.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<ul>
	<li><u><strong>Middle School Concrete Trellis Removal - June 2027 through August 2027</strong></u>: This work would be scheduled during the summer when students and staff are not in the building.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<ul>
	<li><u><strong>Middle School Auditorium - September 2027 through February 2028</strong></u>: Because the work can be contained within the auditorium and accessed from the exterior, construction could continue during the school year.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<ul>
	<li><u><strong>HVAC Improvements - October 2027 through August 2028</strong></u>: Work would be phased around school operations, with larger equipment installations planned for summer 2028.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<p>Planning and design for certain projects would begin shortly after the referendum. The proposed timeline is structured to ensure efficient project sequencing, accommodate construction and equipment lead times, and minimize disruptions to the regular school day. Please note that this preliminary schedule is subject to change based on final designs, bidding results, construction conditions, and contractor availability.</p>

<p>For more information on the schedule and projects, please explore this webpage.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</div>
	



	</div>
	
	<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-2 fsStyleColumn-last fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8934"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8935" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8935" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<article class="fsResource fsResourceTypeImage"><figure><picture><img alt="Red-and-white referendum graphic titled “Proposed Project Timeline,” listing school construction and renovation projects from 2027 to 2028, with a West Essex logo and website." data-aspect-ratio="1.25" data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1792775023/westexorg/pee7ghhtux40trqg9wi6/OCT23.png%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1792775023/westexorg/pee7ghhtux40trqg9wi6/OCT23.png%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1792775023/westexorg/pee7ghhtux40trqg9wi6/OCT23.png%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1792775023/westexorg/pee7ghhtux40trqg9wi6/OCT23.png%22,%22width%22:1080}]" data-permitted-user="true" data-resource-title="OCT23.png" data-resource-uuid="7914f20f-bb7c-4c63-aee2-3e6b54726776"></picture></figure></article>
	</div>


