	</section>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8908" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8908"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8908' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8908'>10/15/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 11</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8908"></a>
	<div class="fsElement fsContainer callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8910" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<section class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_8911" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h3 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8911">Update 28 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 11 About Preparing to Vote Early or on Election Day (October 16, 2026)</h3>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>Over several months, we have shared information about the Nov. 3 bond referendum. Now, it is time for all four of our sending communities to vote.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Whether you reside in Essex Fells, Fairfield, North Caldwell, or Roseland, your vote impacts the future of West Essex. If both ballot questions are approved the district will unlock $9.3 million in state aid to help offset the costs and reduce the tax impact.</p>

<h4>If You Received a Vote By Mail Ballot</h4>

<p>It must be postmarked for return by Tuesday, Nov. 3 to count. You can also drop it in a designated local ballot box:&nbsp;</p>

<ul>
	<li>Essex Fells: Post Office, 297 Runnymede Rd&nbsp;</li>
	<li>Fairfield: Municipal Building, 230 Fairfield Rd&nbsp;</li>
	<li>North Caldwell: Borough Hall, 141 Gould Ave&nbsp;</li>
	<li>Roseland: Municipal Courts Building, 15 Harrison Ave&nbsp;</li>
	<li>Verona: Community Center, 880 Bloomfield Ave</li>
</ul>

<h4>If You Plan to Vote Early In Person</h4>

<p>Sites are open Saturday, Oct. 24 through Sunday, Nov. 1, including at the Fairfield Community Center (221 Hollywood Ave) and Verona Community Center (880 Bloomfield Ave). &nbsp;Early voting sites are open from 10 a.m. to 8 p.m. Monday through Saturday and 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. Sunday. Registered voters can cast a ballot at any designated early voting site in the county.</p>

<h4>If You Plan to Vote In Person on Election Day</h4>

<p>Look up your polling location here. Polls will be open from 6 a.m. to 8 p.m.&nbsp;</p>

<h4>If You Are Told You Cannot Vote For Any Reason</h4>

<p>Ask for a provisional ballot. This ensures your vote can be counted once the mailed ballots are processed and your voter eligibility is double-checked.</p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Every vote matters in this referendum &ndash; make your voice heard!</strong></p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>We look forward to sharing election results at <a href="https://www.westex.org/vote" title="Link takes you to referendum voter information page">www.westex.org/vote</a>.</strong></p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsLayout fsTwoColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8912" data-use-new="true" >

						<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-1 fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8913"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8914" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8914" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<article class="fsResource fsResourceTypeImage"><figure><picture><img alt="Large black text announcing in-person early voting dates and hours is set against a white background with a red header and footer, featuring sample ballot documents and a school logo." data-aspect-ratio="0.5625" data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1792186203/westexorg/rnnh7qwrzb5t8zcuubks/In-PersonEarlyVoting.png%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1792186203/westexorg/rnnh7qwrzb5t8zcuubks/In-PersonEarlyVoting.png%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1792186203/westexorg/rnnh7qwrzb5t8zcuubks/In-PersonEarlyVoting.png%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1792186203/westexorg/rnnh7qwrzb5t8zcuubks/In-PersonEarlyVoting.png%22,%22width%22:1200},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_5/v1792186203/westexorg/rnnh7qwrzb5t8zcuubks/In-PersonEarlyVoting.png%22,%22width%22:1600},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1792186203/westexorg/rnnh7qwrzb5t8zcuubks/In-PersonEarlyVoting.png%22,%22width%22:1920}]" data-permitted-user="true" data-resource-title="In-PersonEarlyVoting.png" data-resource-uuid="3d0d7f8e-1d31-4f08-871d-054a4f04a9ba"></picture></figure></article>
	</div>


	</div>
	



	</div>
	
	<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-2 fsStyleColumn-last fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8915"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8916" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8916" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<article class="fsResource fsResourceTypeImage"><figure><picture><img alt="A political flyer regarding a school district bond referendum features a sample ballot and explanatory text on the left, with large %22VOTE BY MAIL%22 instructions and a red banner at the bottom." data-aspect-ratio="0.5625" data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1792186206/westexorg/crzmvxzgg1qauerq3fow/VotingByMail.png%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1792186206/westexorg/crzmvxzgg1qauerq3fow/VotingByMail.png%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1792186206/westexorg/crzmvxzgg1qauerq3fow/VotingByMail.png%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1792186206/westexorg/crzmvxzgg1qauerq3fow/VotingByMail.png%22,%22width%22:1200},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_5/v1792186206/westexorg/crzmvxzgg1qauerq3fow/VotingByMail.png%22,%22width%22:1600},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1792186206/westexorg/crzmvxzgg1qauerq3fow/VotingByMail.png%22,%22width%22:1920}]" data-permitted-user="true" data-resource-title="VotingByMail.png" data-resource-uuid="a17b360f-6e89-4bb9-b3ed-adce25cf3741"></picture></figure></article>
	</div>


	</div>
	



	</div>
	




	</div>
	


	</div>


	</div>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8897" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8897"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8897' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8897'>10/9/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 10 & Video</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8897"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8899" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8899">Update 27 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 10 with Video About Proposed WEHS Media Center Lab (October 9, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<div style="text-align: center;"><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="315" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Rrlq0wtBYVw?si=a1Uz7pfuUaKRuEDG" title="YouTube video player" width="560"></iframe></div>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>This week, we are highlighting another learning space included in the proposed Nov. 3 bond referendum: <strong>The West Essex High School Media Center</strong>.</p>

<p>The current media center, the heart of our school, has remained largely unchanged since the <strong>1960s</strong>. While it continues to serve our students and staff each day, its aging layout, furnishings, and design no longer fully support the collaborative, creative, and hands-on learning experiences that prepare our students for the future.</p>

<p>The proposed renovation would create a more flexible and welcoming environment for research, independent learning, classroom collaboration, student activities, meetings, presentations, and professional development. The design includes flexible workspaces, movable furniture, improved sight lines, and areas that could accommodate students who participate in a variety of academic and school activities.</p>

<p>In this <a href="https://youtu.be/Rrlq0wtBYVw?si=rXEX1gEwcJfk0XuE" target="_blank" title="Link takes you to YouTube video about West Essex Media Center renovation.">short video</a>, West Essex High School Principal Dr. Kimberly Westervelt takes a closer look at the current Media Center and shares how the proposed renovation could better support students and staff members while creating more opportunities to use this space throughout the school day.</p>

<p>For more information, please explore this referendum page.</p>

<p>Thank you for continuing to stay informed.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8887" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8887"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8887' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8887'>10/2/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 9 & Video</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8887"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8889" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8889">Update 26 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 9 with Video About Proposed Journalism Lab (October 2, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<div style="text-align: center;"><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="315" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZavYO3AuRLk?si=rPKFPJwFO2H7cuzI" title="YouTube video player" width="560"></iframe></div>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>As we continue sharing information about the proposed November 3 bond referendum, we would like to take a closer look at one of the learning spaces included in the proposal: the West Essex High School Journalism Lab.</p>

<p>The current Journalism Lab was originally designed as a computer lab and is limited in both size and flexibility. The proposed renovation would create a larger, collaborative environment designed for writing, editing, broadcasting, photography, and digital media production.</p>

<p>Students in this program produce both the print and digital editions of The Wessex Wire, the school&rsquo;s student-run newspaper. Each season, students also conduct interviews and produce promotional videos for athletic teams during Media Day, gaining valuable hands-on experience in journalism, digital media, and multimedia storytelling. Journalism II further enhances the program by offering students the opportunity to earn dual credit through Montclair State University.</p>

<p>In this <a href="https://youtu.be/ZavYO3AuRLk?si=Wh87-koIx2JddLiL" target="_blank" title="Link takes you to Referendum video on Youtube">short video</a>, West Essex High School Principal Dr. Westervelt takes us inside the current Journalism Lab and shares how the proposed space could enhance student learning and expand hands-on experiences.</p>

<p>For more details about the proposal and how to cast your ballot, please explore the resources on this webpage.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8884" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8884"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8884' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8884'>9/25/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 8 & Video</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8884"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8886" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8886">Update 25 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 8 with Video About Looking Forward to November 3rd (September 25, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<div style="text-align: center;"><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="315" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/eVZfm0CnaJY?si=Vu79ImO_uihyYszi" title="YouTube video player" width="560"></iframe></div>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>Over the past several weeks, we have shared information about the proposed bond referendum, including projects focused on our learning spaces, safety and security, infrastructure, and community facilities. We have also provided information about the financial strategy behind the proposal and the use of a bond referendum to fund these improvements.</p>

<p>Planning for these projects began several years ago and has included the work of architects, engineers, financial advisors, district staff, and the Board of Education. Throughout this process, our commitment has remained the same: to provide clear, accurate, and transparent information so residents can make informed decisions.</p>

<p>We will continue to share information with our community through district communications, Board of Education meetings, local publications, printed materials, and the <a href="https://www.westex.org/referendum" title="Link takes you to referendum page">West Essex Referendum Page</a>.</p>

<p>As an additional resource, the district has created a <a href="https://youtu.be/eVZfm0CnaJY?si=78q1BkHpCtmzoB2t" target="_blank" title="Link takes you to referendum video on youtube">Referendum Video</a> that provides an overview of the proposal and a closer look at the facilities and spaces included in the plan. It also highlights how the proposed improvements would support district programs and the student experience.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Thank you for taking the time to stay informed and engaged throughout this process. We appreciate your continued partnership and involvement in our school community.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8688" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8688"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8688' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8688'>9/18/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 7</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8688"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8690" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8690">Update 24 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 7 About Spaces That Bring Our Community Together (September 18, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>Throughout our district, shared spaces bring students, families, and community members together for learning, performances, athletics, and events.</p>

<p>The proposed November 3 referendum includes improvements to several of these spaces, with projects focused on functionality, accessibility, and supporting the many ways they are used by our schools and community.</p>

<p>One of those spaces is the middle school auditorium, which remains largely unchanged since the building originally opened. Proposed renovations include air conditioning and updates to the auditorium&rsquo;s audio, lighting, technology, and storage. These improvements would support a wide range of student performances, school programs, and community events.</p>

<p>Accessibility is also an important part of the proposed renovations. Improvements such as ramps and railings would make the auditorium more accessible for students, staff members, families, and community members.</p>

<p>The referendum also includes proposed improvements to outdoor athletic spaces, including replacing grass fields with artificial turf, as well as new stadium bleachers and a press box. The fields are used by students in grades 7 through 12 for physical education, along with the marching band, extracurricular programs, athletics, and community organizations. From the school day into the evening, these spaces serve students, families, and visitors throughout the year.</p>

<p>Together, these proposed projects are intended to improve the functionality and accessibility of spaces that are used by both our schools and the broader community.</p>

<p>Thank you for your continued engagement and for taking the time to learn about the proposed referendum.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>

	</div>


	</section>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsLayout fsTwoColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8691" data-use-new="true" >

