	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8582" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8582"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8582' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8582'>9/4/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 5</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8582"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8584" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8584">Update 22 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 5 About Proposed Safety Upgrades (September 4, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>Providing safe and secure schools remains one of the district&rsquo;s highest priorities, and the proposed referendum reflects that commitment. Several projects included in the proposal are designed to strengthen school security while maintaining welcoming and supportive learning environments for our students and staff.</p>

<p>School safety and security projects qualify for the maximum level of state aid. As a result, approximately one-third of the eligible project costs would be covered by the state, helping to reduce the impact on local taxpayers. This state aid is available only with voter approval of the referendum.</p>

<p>Proposed upgrades include secure entrance vestibules at both schools, replacement of aging exterior and interior doors, updated door hardware, and keyless access systems fully integrated with the district&rsquo;s security network.</p>

<p>These enhancements reflect current school safety best practices and would provide staff with greater control over building access while strengthening the district&rsquo;s ability to respond effectively in an emergency. They would also allow designated areas of our schools to be secured quickly when necessary.</p>

<p>Maintaining safe, secure, and welcoming schools is essential to supporting student learning and sustaining our community&rsquo;s confidence in its school facilities.</p>

<p>Please visit our Referendum page to learn more about the proposal and its projects.</p>

<p>Thank you for your continued partnership in education.</p>

<p>Sincerely,</p>

<p>Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://www.westex.org/p/~board/west-essex-regional-school-district-news/post/weekly-referendum-letter-5" target="_blank" title="Links to article."><span class="button-4">Read More &amp; See Pictures</span></a></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8578" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8578"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8578' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8578'>8/28/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 4</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8578"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8580" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8580">Update 21 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 4 & Video About Proposed HS Addition (August 28, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,</p>

<p>Today&#39;s schools require learning spaces that support collaboration, technology, and a variety of instructional programs. The reputation of our high-achieving district speaks for itself; we are consistently ranked among the top places to learn and work in New Jersey. Our students are successful, and to prepare them for their next steps, our programs are constantly evolving.&nbsp;</p>

<p>However, West Essex needs more space at the high school to support its commitment to innovation and opportunity. Currently, many teachers share classrooms throughout the school day because instructional space is limited. This reduces scheduling flexibility and limits opportunities to expand programs.&nbsp;</p>

<p>The referendum includes a two-story classroom addition, a renovated media center, and a modern journalism lab designed to support today&#39;s students while providing versatility for the future.&nbsp;</p>

<p>The additional classrooms would also support small-group instruction, student services, standardized testing requirements, and the continued growth of specialized programs such as WE Thrive.&nbsp;</p>

<p>These projects are intended to provide students and staff with learning environments that reflect the high-quality educational experience our community expects and deserves.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Hear directly from WEHS Principal Dr. Kimberly Westervelt about how these improvements would benefit our students (see below).</p>

<p>Thank you for staying informed.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Sincerely,<br />
Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsEmbed callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8581" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h3 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8581">Watch The Video</h3>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
		    <iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="600" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/kOMASuk96M8?si=rHNUyY1efGfpaUY2" title="YouTube video player" width="900"></iframe>

	</div>


	</section>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8532" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8532"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8532' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8532'>8/21/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 3</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8532"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8534" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8534">Update 20 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 3 About Maximizing State Aid (August 21, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,&nbsp;</p>

<p>One important benefit of using a bond referendum to fund school improvement projects is state aid. Every New Jersey taxpayer contributes to the revenue that helps support school improvement projects. However, districts can only access these funds if voters approve a referendum. That means every time a district passes a referendum in New Jersey, your tax dollars help pay for it.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
We are pleased to share that the New Jersey Department of Education has approved approximately $9.3 million in state aid for both questions being proposed by West Essex. This includes $8.3 million for Question 1 and $1 million for Question 2. This funding helps reduce the amount that must be financed by local taxpayers, while allowing the district to complete important facility improvements.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Without voter approval, our district would continue paying for eligible improvements entirely through local funding, while other communities receive state assistance for similar projects. Although not every project qualifies for state aid, West Essex has an opportunity to bring significant tax dollars back to our communities and offset the local cost of the proposed improvements.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
The estimated monthly tax impact for Question 1 is $21 in Essex Fells, $15 in Fairfield, $22 in North Caldwell, and $15 in Roseland based on the average assessed home in each municipality. &nbsp;</p>

<p>If Question 2 is also approved, the additional estimated monthly impact would be $4 in Essex Fells, $3 in Fairfield, $4 in North Caldwell, and $3 in Roseland. &nbsp;</p>

<p>The estimated tax impact is based on the average assessed home, which is: $947,342 for Essex Fells; $530,788 for Fairfield; $800,484 for North Caldwell; and $639,995 for Roseland. Assessed value is different and typically less than market value. &nbsp;</p>

<p>Additional information about the proposed projects, state aid, estimated tax impact, and how to determine your home&rsquo;s assessed value is available on this webpage.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Thank you for staying informed.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Sincerely,<br />
Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsLayout fsTwoColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8535" data-use-new="true" >

						<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-1 fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8536"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8537" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8537" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
