	</div>


	</div>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8538" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8538" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<article class="fsResource fsResourceTypeImage"><figure><picture><img alt="Infographic for West Essex school bond referendum Question 2: $7.5M projects, including bleachers, press box, doors and hardware." data-aspect-ratio="0.5625" data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1787347266/westexorg/tdk7yd30fgc8rt4z6cd0/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting2.png%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1787347266/westexorg/tdk7yd30fgc8rt4z6cd0/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting2.png%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1787347266/westexorg/tdk7yd30fgc8rt4z6cd0/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting2.png%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1787347266/westexorg/tdk7yd30fgc8rt4z6cd0/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting2.png%22,%22width%22:960}]" data-permitted-user="true" data-resource-title="PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting2.png" data-resource-uuid="d1bfbeb7-2c06-4ea8-abbf-6ac0acfcf1da"></picture></figure></article>
	</div>


	</div>
	



	</div>
	
	<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-2 fsStyleColumn-last fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8539"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8540" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8540" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<article class="fsResource fsResourceTypeImage"><figure><picture><img alt="West Essex Regional School District infographic: Fall 2026 bond referendum donut chart shows $42M in projects, $8.3M state aid, and school upgrades." data-aspect-ratio="0.5625" data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1787347211/westexorg/sg5hrpmjm03mdixg1sxt/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting1.png%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1787347211/westexorg/sg5hrpmjm03mdixg1sxt/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting1.png%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1787347211/westexorg/sg5hrpmjm03mdixg1sxt/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting1.png%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1787347211/westexorg/sg5hrpmjm03mdixg1sxt/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting1.png%22,%22width%22:960}]" data-permitted-user="true" data-resource-title="PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting1.png" data-resource-uuid="6006067d-0a49-41cf-822f-74549bd9c1f4"></picture></figure></article>
	</div>


	</div>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8541" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8541" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<article class="fsResource fsResourceTypeImage"><figure><picture><img alt="Infographic for West Essex Regional School District’s Nov. 3, 2026 bond referendum shows town tax impacts of $15–$26 monthly and a red footer note." data-aspect-ratio="0.5625" data-image-sizes="[{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1787347300/westexorg/w1wuvhpqcvlajeht03xn/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting3.png%22,%22width%22:256},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1787347300/westexorg/w1wuvhpqcvlajeht03xn/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting3.png%22,%22width%22:512},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1787347300/westexorg/w1wuvhpqcvlajeht03xn/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting3.png%22,%22width%22:800},{%22url%22:%22https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1787347300/westexorg/w1wuvhpqcvlajeht03xn/PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting3.png%22,%22width%22:960}]" data-permitted-user="true" data-resource-title="PresentationforJuly15BOEMeeting3.png" data-resource-uuid="49eee5e2-161b-4f0a-a24b-1110338b0f9a"></picture></figure></article>
	</div>


	</div>
	



	</div>
	




	</div>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8496" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
				<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8496"><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_8496' aria-expanded='false' href='#fs-panel-8496'>8/14/2026 | Weekly Referendum Email 2</a></h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true">
		<a id="fs-panel-8496"></a>
	<section class="fsElement fsContent callout-box-light color-1" id="fsEl_8498" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
				<h4 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_8498">Update 19 - Superintendent & Board President Share Weekly Letter 2 About Fiscal Responsibility (August 14, 2026)</h4>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>Dear West Essex School Community,&nbsp;</p>

<p>You may be wondering why some of the proposed school improvement projects cannot be completed through the annual budget. &nbsp;</p>

<p>The reality is that many projects already are. This week&rsquo;s email will review the district&rsquo;s fiscally responsible approach to maintenance.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Each year, about 10% of our annual budget is dedicated to maintenance projects. Over the past 12 years, the district has invested more than $12 million in school improvements using annual budget funds, capital reserve, and the expertise of our in-house maintenance staff. Every summer, classrooms are renovated, systems are repaired, and facilities are upgraded with no additional cost to the taxpayers. &nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
This proactive approach has allowed us to maintain our schools while keeping our focus on student programs and minimizing tax increases. Our goal is to fix and replace things before they break down and lead to costly emergency repairs.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
However, projects such as major additions, infrastructure replacement, and extensive renovations are simply too large to complete one project at a time through the annual budget.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
An approved referendum would provide upfront funding, so critical improvements can be completed over a few years rather than decades. If voters approve, many of the projects included in the referendum would qualify for state aid to offset the tax impact. We don&rsquo;t receive that benefit if we complete projects through the budget or capital reserve funds.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Thank you for taking the time to learn more about this important process.</p>

<p>Sincerely,<br />
Damion Macioci, <em>Superintendent of Schools</em><br />
Maryadele Wojtowicz, <em>Board of Education President</em></p>


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<div class="fsElement fsLayout fsThreeColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8499" data-use-new="true" >

						<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleColumn fsStyleColumn-1 fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_8500"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsResourceElement fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_8501" data-use-new="true" data-source-element-id="8501" data-source-page-id="1315" data-display-items="collections_and_resources" >

